
Problem Statement
Breast cancer is one of the most common diseases affecting women worldwide. Early detection can significantly improve treatment outcomes and survival rates. In this project, we build a machine learning model to predict whether a tumor is benign (non-cancerous) or malignant (cancerous) based on medical features such as radius, texture, perimeter, area, and smoothness.

Objectives
Perform data preprocessing and cleaning.
Apply classification algorithms: SVM, KNN, and Tree-based models (Random Forest).
Evaluate model performance using metrics like Accuracy, Confusion Matrix, and Classification Report.
Identify the most accurate model.
