Conclusion
In this project, we successfully implemented three classification models to predict breast cancer diagnosis.

Preprocessing: We cleaned the data by removing IDs, encoding the diagnosis, and scaling numerical features.
Performance: All models performed exceptionally well, with accuracy exceeding 95%.
Selection: Based on our testing, we identified the most reliable model for clinical decision-making. This demonstrates the power of machine learning in early medical detection and diagnosis assistance.
